WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:20.127
Izzie saw Ethan in the hallway ahead of her.

2
00:00:20.128 --> 00:00:23.884
She thought he was nicer than the other boys.

3
00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:30.233
She hoped they could be partners at Kids Central Camp one day.

4
00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:35.384
In the gym Mr. Dunn was sitting at a table.

5
00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:39.218
"What's the string for?" Ethan asked.

6
00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:43.847
"Today we're making friendship bracelets," Mr. Dunn said.

7
00:00:43.848 --> 00:00:47.076
"Friendship bracelets," Izzie thought.

8
00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:50.795
"I could make one for—"

9
00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:55.116
"Bracelets are for girls!" said Bobby.

10
00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:57.746
"No, they're not," Ethan said.

11
00:00:57.747 --> 00:01:01.287
"At my school in California everyone wore them."

12
00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:06.648
"Well, my sister and her friends wear friendship bracelets," Bobby said.

13
00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:09.458
"I think they're goofy."

14
00:01:09.459 --> 00:01:13.515
"They are not goofy," Mr. Dunn said.

15
00:01:13.516 --> 00:01:16.506
"They're part of a meaningful tradition."

16
00:01:16.507 --> 00:01:18.494
He looked at Bobby.

17
00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:23.284
"When a friend gives you a bracelet, you should never cut it off.

18
00:01:23.285 --> 00:01:28.220
You wear it for as long as the two of you remain friends."

19
00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:32.303
"I can't wait to make mine!" said Izzie.

20
00:01:32.304 --> 00:01:37.237
"First choose three colors," Mr. Dunn instructed.

21
00:01:37.238 --> 00:01:39.074
"This is pretty."

22
00:01:39.075 --> 00:01:42.052
Izzie reached for a bundle of blue thread.

23
00:01:42.053 --> 00:01:46.792
But her hand bumped into another hand reaching for the same one.

24
00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:51.460
"Sorry," Ethan mumbled. "I'll pick a different one."

25
00:01:51.461 --> 00:01:55.400
"You can choose the same color," Mr. Dunn said.

26
00:01:55.401 --> 00:02:02.535
"Izzie, measure out sixty centimeters, and then give Ethan the thread."

27
00:02:02.536 --> 00:02:10.292
Everyone measured and cut six strands of thread.

28
00:02:10.293 --> 00:02:13.259
Then Mr. Dunn showed them what to do.

29
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.342
"Now tie a knot ten centimeters from one end.

30
00:02:17.343 --> 00:02:20.410
Next tape that end to the table.

31
00:02:20.411 --> 00:02:24.605
After that separate the strands by color.

32
00:02:24.606 --> 00:02:28.266
There should be two strands of each color."

33
00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:31.915
"Now we're ready to weave!" said Nina.

34
00:02:31.916 --> 00:02:37.920
Mr. Dunn nodded. "Start with the strand all the way to the left.

35
00:02:37.921 --> 00:02:41.770
Use it to tie a knot around the string next to it.

36
00:02:41.771 --> 00:02:45.678
Keep going all the way across.

37
00:02:45.679 --> 00:02:52.426
Once you've knotted each string, start again on the left.

38
00:02:52.427 --> 00:02:56.266
Do you understand?" Mr. Dunn asked.

39
00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.565
"Yep!" Izzie said.

40
00:02:58.566 --> 00:03:01.352
This looked like it would take a while.

41
00:03:01.353 --> 00:03:04.284
She wanted to finish hers today.

42
00:03:04.285 --> 00:03:12.581
"Weave away! Ask me if you need help," said Mr. Dunn.

43
00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:17.880
"I'm making mine for you," Nina whispered to Izzie.

44
00:03:17.881 --> 00:03:20.822
Izzie looked at her friend and swallowed.

45
00:03:20.823 --> 00:03:24.759
"Thanks." Then she got back to work.

46
00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:32.634
Knot, knot, knot. Knot, knot, knot. Start again.

47
00:03:32.635 --> 00:03:36.455
Finally she was done.

48
00:03:36.456 --> 00:03:41.018
Izzie's hands were cramping and her neck hurt from bending over.

49
00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:43.651
But her bracelet looked great.

50
00:03:43.652 --> 00:03:52.252
"Okay, campers. Time to get out into that sunshine and play some kickball," Mr. Dunn said.

51
00:03:52.253 --> 00:03:58.009
"If you're not done with your bracelets, you can finish them at home," Mr. Dunn added.

52
00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.436
He leaned over and looked at Izzie's bracelet.

53
00:04:01.437 --> 00:04:04.499
"Nice job, Izzie," he said.

54
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.611
"You worked hard today."

55
00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:09.315
"Thanks," said Izzie.

56
00:04:09.316 --> 00:04:12.058
She was glad she was finished.

57
00:04:12.059 --> 00:04:18.240
When everything was put away, the kids lined up to go outside.

58
00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:21.808
Izzie was behind Ethan at the end of the line.

59
00:04:21.809 --> 00:04:26.955
She saw Ethan stuff his unfinished bracelet in his pocket.

60
00:04:26.956 --> 00:04:30.099
"Hey, Ethan." Izzie poked his arm.

61
00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.740
"I made my bracelet for you.

62
00:04:32.741 --> 00:04:35.689
Will you wear it?" she mumbled.

63
00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:40.621
"Sure. Thanks, that's really nice," he told Izzie.

64
00:04:40.622 --> 00:04:49.349
"Cool." Grinning, Izzie tied the bracelet on his wrist.

65
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:56.077
Then she ran to the blacktop.

66
00:04:56.078 --> 00:05:07.670
[caption_out@
